# Desktop Cursor (Lens System)

Desktop only — mobile uses touch interactions, scroll reveals, and responsive motion instead. Never emulate this cursor on touch devices.

## Behavior

- Intelligent magnetic lens: smooth interpolation, inertia, physics-based lag
- Soft attraction toward interactive elements (buttons, cards, nav, video controls, timeline, RSVP)
- Gentle snap — never abrupt locking
- Nearby elements subtly react to cursor proximity
- Acts as spotlight/lens revealing depth and interactivity

## Visual

- Circular, glass-like translucent lens with soft blur and subtle glow
- Slight zoom effect; premium, understated; never distracting

## States

| State | Behavior |
|-------|----------|
| Default | Exploration |
| Hover | Gentle expansion |
| CTA | Stronger magnetic pull |
| Video | Play/pause affordance |
| Form | Precise focus feedback |

## Implementation

```tsx
// ✅ Hide custom cursor on touch/coarse pointers
@media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine) { /* enable lens cursor */ }

// ❌ BAD — cursor on mobile
document.body.style.cursor = 'none';
```

Use `requestAnimationFrame` for movement; respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
